      "paragraph_id": "hk_cfi_2022_lai_chee_ying_hcmp_1218_hcal_738_p5",
      "para_no": "5",
      "exact_quote": "A magistrate may issue a warrant authorizing a police officer with such assistants as may be necessary to enter and search any place if the magistrate is satisfied by information on oath that there is reasonable ground for suspecting that any specified evidence is in the place",
      "paragraph_text": "5. Section 2(2) of Schedule 1 of the Implementation Rules in turn provides as follow: “(2) A magistrate may issue a warrant authorizing a police officer with such assistants as may be necessary to enter and search any place if the magistrate is satisfied by information on oath that there is reasonable ground for suspecting that any specified evidence is in the place .” (Emphasis supplied)",
      "chunk_hash": "4445907af7538b0f636274089167327aa153f460140db00ff2b86d0409120d35",
      "quote_verified_against_source": true,
