      "proposition_id": "prop_lai_cfi_2022_jm_construction_challenge_p3",
      "case_id": "hk_cfi_2022_lai_chee_ying_hcmp_1218_hcal_738",
      "case_name": "Lai Chee Ying v Commissioner of Police",
      "neutral_citation": "[2022] HKCFI 2688",
      "paragraph_id": "hk_cfi_2022_lai_chee_ying_hcmp_1218_hcal_738_p3",
      "para_no": "3",
      "exact_quote": "the phrase “ specified evidence ” as defined in section 1 of Schedule 1 of the Implementation Rules somehow does not cover JM",
      "paragraph_text": "3. As can be gleaned from the Form 86, and as confirmed by the plaintiff’s skeleton submissions lodged on 15 August 2022 (“ P Skel ”) and at the hearing, the plaintiff puts forward one sole ground for challenging the validity of the 2022 Warrant, namely, that, as a matter of construction , the phrase “ specified evidence ” as defined in section 1 of Schedule 1 of the Implementation Rules somehow does not cover JM , so that the Magistrate simply did not have the power to order the search and seizure of JM.",
      "chunk_hash": "3ebb332a9e4ef547bf44bbcbcf827bd9d140e1b0fbdef5d5c92b144c929d3357",
      "quote_verified_against_source": true,
      "review_status": "machine_candidate",
