      "para_no": "35",
      "exact_quote": "the police must be able to carry out effective search on anything, including journalistic material, that contains or is likely to contain evidence of an offence endangering national security",
      "paragraph_text": "35. Second, to serve the legislative purpose of furthering the primary objective of the NSL to effectively suppress, prevent and punish offences endangering national security as identified at [17(1)] above, the police must be able to carry out effective search on anything, including journalistic material, that contains or is likely to contain evidence of an offence endangering national security. Were such material excluded from the definition of “specified evidence”, it would unduly limit the scope and hence reduce the effectiveness of police investigation. That would not be conducive to the said legislative purpose.",
